WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.337
You have now completed the main data-cleaning workflow for this course.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:13.092
You learned how to profile messy data, distinguish different missing states, standardize text, validate values,

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:21.107
measure quality, identify duplicate candidates, preserve questionable records for review, use constraints,

00:00:21.107 --> 00:00:29.198
and test updates safely. These skills give us something very important: a more trustworthy and explainable dataset.

00:00:29.855 --> 00:00:34.447
In the next module, we will build on that foundation by reshaping data.

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:42.037
A clean relational table is not always in the best shape for analysis.

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:44.697
Sometimes we need a wide format.

00:00:44.697 --> 00:00:46.217
Sometimes we need a long format.

00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:53.157
We may need to pivot categories into columns, unpivot columns into rows, or change the analytical grain.

00:00:53.157 --> 00:01:01.282
So the next question becomes: once the data is clean, how should we organize it for reporting, comparison,

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:07.178
visualization, and modeling? That is where we will continue in Module 10.
